== structure of P x P
  induced cycles of P x P up to 10 vertices: [(4, 225), (5, 240), (6, 200), (7, 3600), (8, 6300), (9, 14400), (10, 172440)]
  vertex figures (mixed, pureH, pureV): [((3, 3, 3), 6), ((4, 3, 3), 36), ((5, 2, 2), 36), ((5, 2, 3), 54), ((5, 3, 2), 54), ((5, 3, 3), 72), ((6, 2, 2), 144), ((6, 2, 3), 90), ((6, 3, 2), 90), ((6, 3, 3), 42), ((7, 1, 1), 18), ((7, 1, 2), 54), ((7, 1, 3), 18), ((7, 2, 1), 54), ((7, 2, 2), 144), ((7, 2, 3), 36), ((7, 3, 1), 18), ((7, 3, 2), 36), ((8, 1, 1), 36), ((8, 1, 2), 54), ((8, 1, 3), 18), ((8, 2, 1), 54), ((8, 2, 2), 45), ((8, 3, 1), 18)]
  -> every vertex figure has a pure H edge, a pure V edge and at most 8 of the 9 mixed edges
  induced cycles of P: Counter({5: 12, 6: 10})
  maximal families of pairwise properly meeting 5/6-cycles of P: {((5, 6),): 2, ((5, 3), (6, 1)): 20, ((5, 2),): 6}
  Phi(beta) = sum over the 6 complementary pentagon pairs of beta(C,C') vanishes on all symmetric bilinear forms on Z_1(P;Z/2): True
  CHECK structure PASSED
